fected in conditions like obesity, where it can impact metabolic functions and contribute to the overall health of an individual.", "NEYRINCK:Neyrinck is a researcher who studied the effects of broad-spectrum antibiotics on obese rodents and their metabolic alterations.", "DEKZENNE:Dekzenne is a researcher who collaborated with Neyrinck in studying the effects of antibiotics on the microbiota of obese rodents.", "CANI:Cani is a researcher who supports the idea that broad-spectrum antibiotic therapy significantly reduces plasma levels of lipopolysaccharides in animal models.", "MEMBREZ:Membrez is a researcher who studied the effects of antibiotic treatment on genetically obese rodents with insulin resistance.", "H. PYLORI:H. pylori, or Helicobacter pylori, is a bacterium that can infect humans, particularly the stomach. It is often associated with various gastrointestinal diseases, including ulcers, and has implications for iron absorption. Additionally, H. pylori has been mentioned in the context of antibiotic exposure, which may influence weight gain. This bacterium plays a significant role in gastrointestinal health and disease, highlighting its importance in medical research and treatment.", "ANTIBIOTIC THERAPY:Antibiotic therapy is a treatment method employed to combat bacterial infections, frequently initiated empirically in severe cases. This approach involves the use of antibiotics to address infections and has been the subject of research regarding its effects on microbiota and potential weight gain.", "INFECCIONES BACTERIANAS:Infecciones bacterianas refer to bacterial infections that antibiotics are used to treat, which can impact microbiota diversity.", "ALERGIAS:Alergias refer to allergies, which are immune system reactions to specific substances. These reactions can be influenced by various factors, including genetic predispositions and environmental conditions. Additionally, changes in microbiota due to antibiotic use may also play a role in the development of allergies. Among the different types of allergies, food allergies are notable as they represent adverse immune responses to certain foods. These food allergies can manifest in early childhood and may vary in duration and severity over time.", "DIVERSIDAD FILOGENÉTICA:Diversidad filogenética refers to the genetic diversity of microbial communities, which can be altered by antibiotic treatment.", "SISTEMA INMUNE:El sistema inmune es el conjunto de células y mecanismos que protegen al organismo contra infecciones y enfermedades, incluyendo reacciones alérgicas. Este sistema es fundamental para la defensa del cuerpo y su desarrollo en niños puede influir en la prevalencia de alergias. Además, el sistema inmune es una red compleja de células y proteínas que defiende al organismo contra infecciones, y su desarrollo y mantenimiento están influenciados por la microbiota intestinal. Cambios en esta microbiota, como los provocados por el uso de antibióticos, pueden afectar el funcionamiento del sistema inmune.", "ROEDORES:", "GENES CANDIDATOS:Los genes candidatos son aquellos identificados en estudios de asociación que ayudan a entender la sensibilidad y resistencia a la diabetes y obesidad.", "DIVERSIDAD GENÉTICA:La diversidad genética se refiere a las variaciones en los genes entre individuos, lo que puede influir en la susceptibilidad a enfermedades metabólicas."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}